-- =============================================================================
-- ScrapIQ CI — Initial migration (placeholder)
-- =============================================================================
-- This file is a placeholder. The real SQL will be generated by Prisma on the
-- first `bun run db:migrate` (or `bun run db:migrate:prod` against a real
-- PostgreSQL 16 + pgvector instance).
--
-- Why a placeholder?
--   The sandbox has no PostgreSQL instance, so `prisma migrate dev` cannot run
--   here. The migration will be generated during the first deployment against
--   a real Postgres cluster. Once generated, the file `migration.sql` in this
--   folder will contain the full DDL (CREATE TABLE, CREATE INDEX, CREATE TYPE
--   for enums, CREATE EXTENSION vector, etc.).
--
-- Prerequisite on the target Postgres cluster (run as superuser once):
--   CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector;
--
-- After the real migration is generated:
--   - `bun run db:migrate:prod` (== `prisma migrate deploy`) applies every
--     migration file in this folder, in order, to bring the DB schema up to
--     the latest state.
--   - `bun run db:seed:prod` then creates the first OWNER user + Organization.
--
-- Row-Level Security (RLS) policies are NOT generated by Prisma. They must be
-- applied manually after `migrate deploy`. See the `// RLS:` comments in
-- prisma/schema.prisma for the exact CREATE POLICY statements.
-- ============================================================================

-- Initial migration — will be generated by `prisma migrate dev` on first PostgreSQL connection
-- This file is a placeholder. Run `bun run db:migrate` after setting DATABASE_URL to a PostgreSQL instance.
